&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 12pt; line-height: normal; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); vertical-align: baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt&quot;&gt;This occupation is found in all organisations that require oversight of their risk management and internal processes. Organisations that employ Certified Internal Auditors are typically medium to large public, third-sector or private organisations. This includes companies that deal in goods and services, financial institutions, and government departments. Accountancy firms employ Certified Internal Auditors to perform internal audits on behalf of their clients within those clients&#39; businesses and organisations. Companies may employ their own Certified Internal Auditors to perform in-house internal audits. Alternatively, they may choose to outsource their internal audit activities to third parties. In the public sector, an internal audit function will carry out in-house internal audits in organisations such as central government departments, local authorities, regulators, and higher education institutions. Certified Internal Auditors are qualified and recognised globally by the Institute of Internal Auditors (IIA) and in the UK and Ireland by the Chartered Institute of Internal Auditors (CIIA). They carry out their activities with reference to the Global Internal Audit Standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 12pt; line-height: normal; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); vertical-align: baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt&quot;&gt;The broad purpose of the occupation is to provide an independent and objective assurance and advisory service that adds value and improves an organisation&#39;s operations. Certified Internal Auditors support organisations in accomplishing their objectives by bringing a systematic and disciplined approach to evaluating and improving the effectiveness of governance, risk management, and control processes. Internal audit activities assess the adequacy and effectiveness of all areas of an organisation, including risk management, compliance, and financial functions. Internal audit must remain impartial and independent in its work across all areas of the organisation. Certified Internal Auditors are recognised professionals in risk management, internal audit, governance, and control. They are globally recognised as professional internal auditors. They communicate complex concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, ensuring that stakeholders understand audit outcomes and areas for improvement. Certified Internal Auditors provide challenging and sometimes provocative insights into risks and internal controls. They always act independently and objectively, representing the interests of the organisation&#39;s stakeholders. They maintain the highest standards of professional conduct and competence, and they consistently uphold ethical behaviour and integrity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt&quot;&gt;In their daily work, an employee in this occupation interacts with an internal audit team and may manage other internal audit professionals. A Certified Internal Auditor typically reports to an Internal Audit Manager or Chief Audit Executive. They interact with stakeholders across the organisation who have an interest in audit activities, whether they are subject to internal audit activity, receive assurance, or own the outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom: 12pt; line-height: normal; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); vertical-align: baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11.5pt&quot;&gt;An employee in this occupation will work both independently and as part of a team to deliver internal audit engagements. This includes tasks such as planning, testing processes for design, effectiveness, and accuracy, and report writing. Their work is supervised to ensure quality, but they manage their workflow in line with a rigorous methodology and with reference to the Global Internal Audit Standards and sector-specific practice. They ensure that audits are conducted in accordance with the organisation&#39;s internal audit manual.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
